<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Edessa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">260 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-persian-wars">Roman–Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Edessa was fought in 260 CE in upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> between the Roman emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valerian">Valerian</a> and the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-i">Shapur I</a>. The Roman army was defeated and Valerian was captured, the first Roman emperor to be taken prisoner. Shapur commemorated the victory in rock reliefs, and it confirmed the power of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-edessa.jpg" alt="Battle of Edessa" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naghsh-e_rostam,_Ir%C3%A1n,_2016-09-24,_DD_12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
